From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chad Cormier Roussel <chadcormierroussel@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 23:01:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] d3d12: Add a private MetalFX temporal upscale interface.

MacNeutron answers a game's Intel XeSS calls with MetalFX's temporal
upscaler (Wine's libxess.dll). D3D12 had no way to reach it: DXMT's
MetalFX path exists only on D3D11's context. This adds a private one,
in the new src/d3d12/d3d12_interfaces.hpp (plain structs, fixed IIDs
and method order, since Wine keeps a C copy):

- IMTLD3D12DeviceExt, from the device's QueryInterface where MetalFX
  has a temporal scaler: GetTemporalScalerScaleRange, and
  CreateTemporalScaler, which checks the sizes and formats, clamps the
  content scale range to the device's (0: the device's bound) and
  creates the upscaler without waiting for its pipelines. E_INVALIDARG
  for a bad description, E_OUTOFMEMORY when MetalFX makes none.
- IMTLD3D12CommandListExt::TemporalUpscale, on DIRECT and COMPUTE
  lists: checks everything before recording anything (E_INVALIDARG),
  then records a new encoder type that the queue encodes between two
  blits handing over on the upscaler's fence, as the D3D11 path does:
  D3D12 textures are untracked. A depth/stencil depth (or another
  format MetalFX can't read) and typeless motion vectors are copied
  into scratch textures first, and an output MetalFX can't write
  (no ShaderWrite or RenderTarget usage) is written to a scratch
  texture and copied out after, in blits of the list's own. The
  encoder keeps the upscaler and its textures until the allocator
  resets, so the owner may release it right after recording.

winemetal: the temporal scaler's info and properties gain, at their
ends, the reactive mask, macOS 27's output-resolution and jittered
motion vectors and the content offsets; encodeTemporalScale takes the
reactive mask; a new call (150) returns the device's scale range.
D3D11 zero-initialises its info, so the new fields stay off there.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
